.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH pvc-spectralextractor 1  "pvc-spectralextractor " 
.SH NAME
pvc\-spectralextractor \- Periodic/noise spectrum separator: tracks each bin\*(Aqs frame\-to\- frame frequency deviation and gates it on or off depending on whether that deviation stays under a threshold, extracting either the tonal part of a sound or its noise residue
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpvc\-spectralextractor\fR [\fB\-\-fft\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-frames\-per\-sec\fR] [\fB\-\-time\-factor\fR] [\fB\-\-pitch\fR] [\fB\-\-freq\-shift\fR] [\fB\-\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-begin\fR] [\fB\-\-end\fR] [\fB\-\-spectral\-type\fR] [\fB\-\-freq\-change\-threshold\fR] [\fB\-\-freq\-change\-response\fR] [\fB\-\-release\fR] [\fB\-\-complement\fR] [\fB\-\-frame\-norm\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-warp\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-freq\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-freq\fR] [\fB\-\-threshold\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> <\fIOUTPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Periodic/noise spectrum separator: tracks each bin\*(Aqs frame\-to\- frame frequency deviation and gates it on or off depending on whether that deviation stays under a threshold, extracting either the tonal part of a sound or its noise residue.
.PP
Ports `spectralextractor`\*(Aqs audio\-processing path (`legacy/ pvc_src/spectralextractor.c`); see `pvc\-core::tools:: spectralextractor`\*(Aqs doc comment for a real dead pitch/frequency\- shift computation reproduced faithfully, and what\*(Aqs out of scope.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-fft\fR \fI<FFT>\fR [default: 1024]
`\-N`: FFT size (must be a power of two)
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-size\fR \fI<WINDOW_SIZE>\fR [default: 0]
`\-M`: analysis/resynthesis window length. `0` means auto (`2 * fft`, or larger still if needed to fit the resynthesis hop)
.TP
\fB\-\-window\fR \fI<WINDOW>\fR [default: hamming]

.TP
\fB\-\-frames\-per\-sec\fR \fI<FRAMES_PER_SEC>\fR [default: 200]
`\-D`: analysis frames per second (sets the hop size)
.TP
\fB\-\-time\-factor\fR \fI<TIME_FACTOR>\fR [default: 1]
`\-I`: time expansion/contraction factor (`1.0` = unchanged duration)
.TP
\fB\-\-pitch\fR \fI<PITCH>\fR [default: 0]
`\-P`: pitch transposition in semitones \- a plain number, or `@path`. Real, narrow effect only (see `pvc\-core::tools:: spectralextractor`\*(Aqs doc comment): selects oscillator\-bank resynthesis and shifts the shelf\-EQ banding frequency, but never the output\*(Aqs actual pitch
.TP
\fB\-\-freq\-shift\fR \fI<FREQ_SHIFT>\fR [default: 0]
`\-a`: frequency shift adder in Hz \- a plain number, or `@path`. Same narrow real effect as `\-\-pitch` \- see that flag\*(Aqs doc comment
.TP
\fB\-\-gain\fR \fI<GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
`\-A`: gain in dB \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-begin\fR \fI<BEGIN>\fR [default: 0]
`\-b`: begin time in seconds
.TP
\fB\-\-end\fR \fI<END>\fR [default: 0]
`\-e`: end time in seconds (`0` = end of file)
.TP
\fB\-\-spectral\-type\fR \fI<SPECTRAL_TYPE>\fR [default: periodic]
`\-q`: which part of the spectrum to keep
.TP
\fB\-\-freq\-change\-threshold\fR \fI<FREQ_CHANGE_THRESHOLD>\fR [default: 0]
`\-Q`: max (periodic mode) / min (noise mode) frequency change allowed every 5 milliseconds, in Hz \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-freq\-change\-response\fR \fI<FREQ_CHANGE_RESPONSE>\fR [default: 0]
`\-g`: response time of the frequency\-change threshold accumulator, in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-release\fR \fI<RELEASE>\fR [default: 0]
`\-L`: amplitude\-gate release time in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-complement\fR \fI<COMPLEMENT>\fR [default: 0]
`\-c`: complement amplitude spectrum proportion (0\-1) \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-frame\-norm\-limit\fR \fI<FRAME_NORM_LIMIT>\fR [default: 0]
`\-E`: frame normalization decibel limit (`0` disables normalization) \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-warp\fR \fI<WARP>\fR [default: 0]
`\-W`: spectrum magnitude warp index \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-gain\fR \fI<SHELF_LOW_GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
`\-H`: low shelf EQ gain in dB \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-gain\fR \fI<SHELF_HIGH_GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
`\-X`: high shelf EQ gain in dB \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-freq\fR \fI<SHELF_LOW_FREQ>\fR [default: 200]
`\-m`: low shelf EQ frequency in Hz \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-freq\fR \fI<SHELF_HIGH_FREQ>\fR [default: 2000]
`\-R`: high shelf EQ frequency in Hz \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-threshold\fR \fI<THRESHOLD>\fR [default: \-96]
`\-t`: oscillator\-bank resynthesis threshold in dB (only consumed when `\-\-pitch`/`\-\-freq\-shift` select that resynthesis path)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>

.TP
<\fIOUTPUT\fR>

